                  <provenance><orgName role="fmo" key="org_934">Worcester, Parish church of St
                        Helen</orgName><p><q>The calendar prefixed is a Sarum calendar, probably
                           written for the church of St Helen, Worcester, between 1228 and 1224.</q>
                        <bibl>Historical Manuscripts Commission, <title>Report on Manuscripts in
                              Various Collections, Volume IV</title> (1907), pp. 28-29</bibl>, on
                        information from Reverend H. M. Bannister.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_1">Exeter, Devon. Cathedral
                        church of St Peter</orgName><p>In the Calendar, the dedication of the church
                        of Exeter (21 November; s. xiii ex.). The dedication of the church of St
                        Helen's, Worcester (9 June), is in large blue and red capitals. It appears,
                        then, that this was probably written for St Helen's but later moved to
                        Exeter, where it was in the Cathedral s. xiv ex: the lectiones probatoriae
                        agree with the entry for 'unum bonon psalterium' in the list of choir books
                        of 1383.</p><note type="MLGB3_medievalCatalogueNotes">Cat. p.
                     333</note></provenance>
               </history>
